  "excluded": [
    "`type` and `validate` inside an attribute definition are options *of* a column, not columns.",
    "The anonymous `module.exports = (sequelize) => {\u2026}` adds no Function: an anonymous default export has no name a call site uses.",
    "`Player.belongsTo(...)`, `orchestra.hasMany(...)` \u2014 member calls on untyped receivers; they are associations, read as REFERENCES, not CALLS.",
    "`new Sequelize(...)` in `db.js` is a top-level call with no caller to hang a CALLS edge on.",
    "`belongsToMany(venue, { through: 'booking' })` joins through a model named by a *string*, which Sequelize generates at run time: no file declares it, so neither it nor its two keys are labelled, and nothing here is its join model. `booking.js` defines `gig`, an unrelated model the fourth review's text wrongly called the join table (the fifth review's ORM N7)."
